Z||000000||maryjane||10-30-2001||10:09 PM||||Got this in email tonite.<P>Her side of the story:<BR>He was in an odd mood Sunday night. We<BR>planned to meet at a bar for a drink.<BR>I had spent the afternoon shopping with the<BR>girls, & I thought it might have been my<BR>fault because I was a little later than I had promised, but he didn't mention it.<BR>The conversation was very slow going, so I thought we should go off somewhere more intimate where we could talk more privately.<BR>We went to a little restaurant, and he was STILL acting a bit funny. I tried to cheer him up and started wondering if it was me or something else. I asked him, he just said "no". But I wasn't really sure.<BR>So anyway, in the car, on the way back home, I said that I loved him deeply and he just put his arm around me. I didn't know what the hell THAT meant, because, you know, he didn't say it back or anything. We finally get back home, and I'm actually wondering if he was going to leave me! So I tried to get him to talk, but he just turned on the TV.<BR>Reluctanly, I said I was going to bed.<BR>Then after about 10 minutes, he joined me, and to my surprise, we made love. But, he still seemed really distracted, so afterwards I wanted to confront him but instead just cried myself to sleep. I really don't know what to do anymore. I mean,<BR>I really think he's seeing someone else.<P>His side of the story:<BR>The Packers lost. Got laid tho...<p>[This message has been edited by maryjane (edited 10-30-2001).]||||reg||1
